#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049402 :topic/difficulty 1.2146672941862109 :topic/id #uuid "f1be558e-6518-5abd-9478-54113fb37446" :topic/knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115398 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114947 :question/id #uuid "5adf056c-d122-54e6-b55f-5e85d39750c4" :question/math-academy-id "e-207" :question/problem "Calculate $\\dfrac {\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}$ if $y = 2 \\,\\textrm {arccot } x.$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of $\\textrm{arccot}$ is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm d x}(\\textrm {arccot } x) \t=  -\\dfrac 1 {1+x^2}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2\\,\\text{arccot }x) \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\text{arccot }x) \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}\\right) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{1+{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b34b7ab4-a17b-5667-bd2b-5ed53e43afb6" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Inverse Reciprocal Trigonometric Functions"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115399 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114951 :question/id #uuid "99db3f5c-5d6f-5e8e-a31c-a627ddd5c6dc" :question/math-academy-id "e-208" :question/problem "If $f(x) = \\dfrac{\\textrm{arcsec } x}{\\textrm{arccsc } x},$ calculate $f'(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we let $u(x) = \\textrm{arcsec } x$ and $v(x) = \\textrm{arccsc } x$, and apply the quotient rule.\n\nWe use the formulae\n\n$$\nu'(x) =  \\dfrac 1 {|x| \\sqrt {x^2 - 1}}\t\\quad \\text{and} \\quad\tv'(x) = -\\dfrac 1 {|x| \\sqrt {x^2 - 1}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\cdot \\text{arccsc }x-\\text{arcsec }x\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\right)}{{\\text{arccsc }}^{2}x} \\\\  & =\\left(\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\right)\\frac{\\text{arccsc }x+\\text{arcsec }x}{{\\text{arccsc }}^{2}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{arccsc }x+\\text{arcsec }x}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}{\\text{ arccsc }}^{2}x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "20a5f15e-8a26-57af-a867-8f8ae02a91c1" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Inverse Reciprocal Trigonometric Functions Using the Quotient Rule"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115400 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114954 :question/id #uuid "fd6239d1-4fec-50b9-8018-f6e185c4e0d0" :question/math-academy-id "e-209" :question/problem "If $f(x) =3 x\\, \\textrm {arccsc }x,$ calculate $f'(x).$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of $\\textrm{arccsc}$ is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm d x}(\\textrm {arccsc } x) \t=  -\\dfrac 1 {|x| \\sqrt {x^2 - 1}} \\, .\n$$\n\nUsing the product rule and the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3x\\,\\text{arccsc }x) \\\\  & =3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x\\,\\text{arccsc }x) \\\\  & =3(x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\text{arccsc }x)+\\text{arccsc }x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x)) \\\\  & =3x\\left(-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\right)+3\\,\\text{arccsc }x\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-\\frac{3x}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}+3\\,\\text{arccsc }x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "905d1f6a-72aa-5984-8c7d-920497fd58e4" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Inverse Reciprocal Trigonometric Functions Using the Product Rule"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115401 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114956 :question/id #uuid "38c9e8d8-871f-54b1-a8df-637f54430cc1" :question/math-academy-id "e-210" :question/problem "Find $f'(x)$ if $f(x) =2 \\, \\textrm {arccot } (x^2 + 5).$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of $\\textrm{arccot}$ is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm d x}(\\textrm {arccot } x) \t=  -\\dfrac 1 {1+x^2}.\n$$\n\nUsing the chain rule and the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2\\,\\text{arccot }({x}^{2}+5)) \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{1}{1+({x}^{2}+5)^{2}}\\right)\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}+5) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{1+({x}^{2}+5)^{2}}\\cdot 2x \\\\  & =-\\frac{4x}{1+({x}^{2}+5)^{2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{4x}{{x}^{4}+10{x}^{2}+26}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c1def23-83e0-5dc7-b20b-9693127d3a9e" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Inverse Reciprocal Trigonometric Functions Using the Chain Rule"}] :topic/math-academy-id 1721 :topic/next [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048999} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049311} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049533}] :topic/title "Differentiating Inverse Reciprocal Trigonometric Functions"}]}
